#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# doc: migrated from tests/fixtures/none_literal_forward_callee.gg (run_gg pair)
# expect:
#   exit: 0
#   stdout: "7\n"
#!end
# Latent silent-None class: a bare `None` argument to a NOT-YET-LOWERED
# callee (caller textually BEFORE the callee, single module). The self-host
# lowerer's `get_fn_param_types` scans only already-lowered `gmod.functions`,
# so the expected-type lookup misses and the bare `None` lowers to a zeroed
# `(Option__T){0}` — tag 0 reads as Some → miscompile (OBSERVED through the
# self-host runtime_diff: mis-runs/CRASHes on this shape; the scout's earlier
# minimal variant printed 0 — same zeroed-tag class. Rust prints 7 — correct).
# Rust gg registers fn sigs in a typed
# pre-pass (`src/ir/lowering/functions.rs:659-669`), so lowering order does
# not matter there. Expected output below is the CORRECT (Rust) behavior;
# the self-host gap is tracked in TODO.md ("param-type pre-pass" fix).
#
# Sibling fixtures: none_literal_at_call_arg.gg (primitive payload),
# none_literal_at_call_arg_resource.gg (resource payload, callee-first).

public struct Tag:
    Option[String] label

void main():
    print(reach(None))

int reach(Option[String] o):
    match o:
        case Some(s):
            return s.len()
        case None:
            return 7
